{"engine_version":"0.29.2","file":"lunar-time-budget.toml","toml":"# Coordinated Lunar Time (LTC) end-to-end time-error budget over a tau grid.\n#\n# A single averaging-time (tau) error table invites the objection \"you picked the tau that\n# flatters your clock.\" This scenario answers it: the seven LTC error terms are assembled as\n# time-error curves x_i(tau) (seconds) across a whole grid of averaging times, root-summed into\n# x_Sigma(tau), and the clock-vs-frame CROSSOVER tau is located — the tau at which the growing\n# clock term overtakes the constant real-time frame-realisation term. Below the crossover the\n# budget is frame-limited (the reference-frame realisation dominates, not the clock); above it the\n# clock dominates. Where the crossover falls depends entirely on the clock class — for the default\n# passive H-maser it is far out in tau, for a coarse mini-RAFS it is seconds — which is exactly why\n# a single-tau number is misleading. (src/lunar_time_budget.rs)\n#\n# Honesty: MODELLED. The tau-slopes are closed-form and analytically checkable (clock tau^{+1/2}\n# or tau^{+1}, floors tau^0, measurement tau^{-1/2}) and the clock rows reproduce the published\n# one-day clock specs; but the RF/optical-link, frame-realisation, relativistic-residual and\n# ephemeris floor MAGNITUDES are Modelled budget allocations (documented defaults, caller-\n# overridable), not measurements. The contribution is the reproducible crossover tau, not a\n# certified per-term number. Nothing here is certified for operational timekeeping.\nkind = \"lunar-time-budget\"\n\n# On-board clock class driving the (growing) clock term. One of:\n#   optical-master | passive-h-maser | rafs | mini-rafs\nclock = \"passive-h-maser\"\n\n# The averaging-time (tau) grid is the default 1 s ... 1e7 s log-spaced grid (8 points/decade).\n# Uncomment to override:\n# tau_min_s = 1.0\n# tau_max_s = 1.0e7\n# points_per_decade = 8\n","summary":"lunar-time-budget | clock passive-h-maser | 7-term x_Σ(τ) over 57 τ-points (1–1e7 s) | crossover τ 8.689e4 s (x 1.001e-9 s) | frame floor 1.001e-9 s | clock x(1 d) 0.995 ns (MODELLED)","json":"{\n  \"clock\": \"passive-h-maser\",\n  \"clock_crossovers\": [\n    {\n      \"clock\": \"optical-master\",\n      \"closed_form_rel_diff\": 0.0,\n      \"crossover_tau_s\": 9606645.961713081,\n      \"crossover_tau_s_closed_form\": 9606645.961713081,\n      \"noise_type\": \"flicker-fm\",\n      \"sigma_y_one_s\": 1.0416666644973457e-16,\n      \"x_one_day_s\": 8.999999981257068e-12\n    },\n    {\n      \"clock\": \"passive-h-maser\",\n      \"closed_form_rel_diff\": 0.0,\n      \"crossover_tau_s\": 86894.28467734443,\n      \"crossover_tau_s_closed_form\": 86894.28467734443,\n      \"noise_type\": \"flicker-fm\",\n      \"sigma_y_one_s\": 1.1516203733194e-14,\n      \"x_one_day_s\": 9.950000025479615e-10\n    },\n    {\n      \"clock\": \"rafs\",\n      \"closed_form_rel_diff\": 5.449420488347446e-16,\n      \"crossover_tau_s\": 10013.850504482569,\n      \"crossover_tau_s_closed_form\": 10013.850504482563,\n      \"noise_type\": \"white-fm\",\n      \"sigma_y_one_s\": 1.0000000000000001e-11,\n      \"x_one_day_s\": 2.9393876913398138e-9\n    },\n    {\n      \"clock\": \"mini-rafs\",\n      \"closed_form_rel_diff\": 3.52207401338621e-16,\n      \"crossover_tau_s\": 3.7826224675764633,\n      \"crossover_tau_s_closed_form\": 3.782622467576462,\n      \"noise_type\": \"white-fm\",\n      \"sigma_y_one_s\": 5.145221229451655e-10,\n      \"x_one_day_s\": 1.5123799951070498e-7\n    }\n  ],\n  \"crossover_tau_s\": 86894.28467734443,\n  \"crossover_x_s\": 1.0006922855944562e-9,\n  \"frame_term_s\": 1.0006922855944562e-9,\n  \"kind\": \"lunar-time-budget\",\n  \"label\": \"MODELLED end-to-end LTC time-error budget. The τ-slopes are closed-form and analytically checkable (clock τ^{+1/2}/τ^{+1}, floors τ^0, measurement τ^{-1/2}) and the clock rows reproduce the published one-day clock specs; the RF/optical link, frame-realisation, relativist